  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/chapalichthys_pardalis_en/",
      "html": "<p>The Polkadot Goodeid, Chapalichthys pardalis, reaches a maximum length of 6.5 cm (males) and 7 cm (females). It is a livebearing species.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/chapalichthys_pardalis_en/",
      "html": "<p>In the aquarium, however, it is a top rarity. Sadly the fish grow rather slowly, which makes them a bit more expensive. On the other hand, the fish become more beautiful with growing age.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/chapalichthys_pardalis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Its natural habitat is the waters of the Pacific slope of Mexico, Michoacán province, Tocumbo district. In contrast to many other goodeids, this pretty livebearing species seems not to be endangered in the wild.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "maintenance",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/chapalichthys_pardalis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Keeping and breeding of the fish is not difficult. However, it is best to keep them under slightly varying temperatures and (in living rooms) without a heater, because in the wild the temperature hardly ever rises above 20°C. The fish looks best in tanks with dense vegetation.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/chapalichthys_pardalis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Towards tankmates, at least the strain currently present in the hobby is said to be very peaceful.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/chapalichthys_pardalis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Lexicon: Chapalichthys means \"fish from Lake Chapala\". Lake Chapala in Mexico is the habitat of one species of Chapalichthys. pardalis is Latin and means \"painted like a panther\".</p>"
    }
  ],
